@body

![Challenge problem 2](assets/source_fidelity/lect07c/image_001.png)

- probability short tail/tailless (Tt)\: 2/3
- probability long tail (tt)\: 1/3

![Punnett square](assets/source_fidelity/lect07c/punnett_lethal_tt.svg)

@notes

Source: lect07c-prob_of_progeny_2.odp, slide 6.
Verified against original: one Punnett square, with the lethal-TT cross restored where present.

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 3](assets/source_fidelity/lect07c/image_001.png)

- probability short tail/tailless (Tt)\: 2/3
- probability long tail (tt)\: 1/3
- k is number of short tail mice\:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\binom{5}{k}\times\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^k\cdot\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{5-k}
&=\binom{5}{k}\times 2^k\cdot\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^k\cdot\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{5-k}\\
&=\binom{5}{k}\times 2^k\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^5
\end{aligned}
$$

![Slide image 4](assets/source_fidelity/lect07c/image_004.png)

@notes

Source: lect07c-prob_of_progeny_2.odp, slide 7.
