# Exact Monohybrid Crosses

@notes

Source: lect07c-prob_of_progeny_2.odp, slide 26.

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 17](assets/source_fidelity/lect07c/image_017.png)

- Problem\: there is a 75% chance of A&#8211; and only 25% chance of aa.

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\binom{4}{3}\cdot0.75^3\cdot(1-0.75)^{4-3}\\
&=\left(\frac{4!}{3!\cdot(4-3)!}\right)\cdot0.75^3\cdot(0.25)^1\\
&=\left(\frac{4}{1}\right)\cdot0.75^3\cdot0.25=4\cdot0.421875\cdot0.25\\
&=0.421875
\end{aligned}
$$

@notes

Source: lect07c-prob_of_progeny_2.odp, slide 27.
Layout revised against original; selected equations authored in LaTeX and rendered as measured SVG.

